Keep the match stack between searches (succinctly #7965)

Every `onig_search` starts `match_at` on a 160-entry stack that `alloca` gives it, and
`STACK_SAVE` copies that stack into a fresh `xmalloc` when `match_at` returns, so the next start
position of the same search can reuse it; `MATCH_ARG_FREE` frees it when the search ends. A
search per match is one `malloc`, one copy of a few KB and one `free`, which jq pays as well and
which was most of the cost of a many-match `gsub`/`scan`/`split` in `succinctly jq` (#7965).

This keeps the saved stack in the `OnigMatchParam` when the search ends, and the next search
with the same parameter starts from it, exactly as a later start position of one search starts
from the stack an earlier one saved. Only a stack laid out for the same number of pointers
(`ptr_num`) is taken. `onig_free_match_param_content` frees a kept stack, so `onig_search`'s own
stack-local parameter still frees everything it allocated. No answer changes: the regex corpus
gate (`scripts/jq-regex-corpus.py`) passes unchanged.

Apply from `vendor/oniguruma` with `patch -p1 < patches/0001-keep-the-match-stack-between-searches.patch`.

--- a/src/regexec.c	2026-11-28 01:24:43
+++ b/src/regexec.c	2026-11-28 01:24:43
